==============================================


pmca — Sony-PMCA-RE by ma1co
  https://github.com/ma1co/Sony-PMCA-RE
  License: MIT
  Only the usb/, util/ and backup/ subpackages are included.

pyusb
  https://github.com/pyusb/pyusb
  License: BSD (see src/vendor/usb/LICENSE if present, otherwise upstream)

libusb-1.0 (libusb_package)
  https://libusb.info/
  License: LGPL-2.1 — bundled as a shared library (src/vendor/libusb_package/libusb-1.0.dll)
  and loaded at runtime via ctypes, not statically linked. Source:
  https://github.com/libusb/libusb

importlib_resources
  https://github.com/python/importlib_resources
  License: Apache-2.0

Cryptodome (shim only)
  pmca imports Cryptodome.Hash.SHA256 and calls SHA256.new(data).digest().
  src/vendor/Cryptodome/ is a three-file stand-in implemented with hashlib,
  not the pycryptodomex distribution. pycryptodomex itself is not bundled.

Firmware-derived strings
========================

src/data/a9_fn_functions.json contains function symbol names and saved-value
bytes read from the public firmware of the ILCE-9 (version 6.00) for the sole
purpose of addressing the camera's own function table.

src/data/a9_fn_chinese_names.json contains 77 Chinese menu labels, 64 of which
were matched against the camera's own Chinese UI resources. These strings are
reproduced only so that the tool shows the same wording the user sees on the
camera. No rights over them are claimed, and no firmware binary, key, or
unpacked firmware artifact is distributed with this project.

