Reference projects
==================

dino2048/ZV-E10-5GHz-WiFi-Unlock
  https://github.com/dino2048/ZV-E10-5GHz-WiFi-Unlock
  The 5 GHz unlock approach is cross-checked against this project. Nothing is
  redistributed from it: the ZV-E10 targets a different configuration number,
  menu library and configuration set, and the A9 change was derived from the
  camera's own firmware and verified on hardware here.

Erlla/sony-a7m4-custom-firmware
  https://github.com/Erlla/sony-a7m4-custom-firmware
  The 17 additional Creative Looks shipped by the R11 build are colour-fitted
  from the LUT and look definitions in this project. No file from it is
  redistributed: the A9 uses its own dual-source property records, generated
  here from that fitting, and only the numeric results travel in the patch.

robinshie/Sony_A7M3
  https://github.com/robinshie/Sony_A7M3
  License: MIT
  Pinned at commit e6bbfafb55570a5de34e75c195e7e1c780d03340.
  The menu-transplant technique (attaching the change to the real menu-creation
  call) originates here. No upstream binary or address table is redistributed;
  the addresses used by this project were re-derived from the ILCE-9 firmware.

